{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-146202",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)]-{\\mu }_{X|1}^{2} \\\\  & =[(1)^{2}\\cdot 0.4+(2)^{2}\\cdot 0.6]-(1.6)^{2} \\\\  & =0.4+2.4-2.56 \\\\  & =0.24.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
